{{!-- Where Microsoft Graph posts change notifications, shown by both Microsoft providers in their MS
Graph API mode. mainServiceUrl comes from the page context. --}}
<div class="space-y-2">
    <p class="text-sm">Microsoft Graph posts change notifications to these two endpoints, which must accept anonymous
        HTTPS <strong>POST</strong> requests from the internet:</p>
    <pre class="ee-code-block"><code>{{mainServiceUrl}}/oauth/msg/lifecycle
{{mainServiceUrl}}/oauth/msg/notification</code></pre>
    <span class="helper-text">If this instance cannot be reached directly, set <a href="/admin/reference/settings#postV1Settings"
            target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link link-animated"><code>notificationBaseUrl</code></a>
        to a public proxy domain, and Graph posts to <code>https://&lt;proxy-domain&gt;/oauth/msg/...</code>
        instead.</span>
</div>
